      "writtenOn": "2023-12-14T11:06:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The node is also used for unprotected VM where pvmfw isn\u0027t involved.\n\nHow? I thought pvIOMMUs were only supported by pKVM for pVMs? What is parsing the VM DTBO\u0027s `/host`, other than `pvmfw`?\n\n\u003e `device` seems better fit compared to `target`, `virtual`, `overlay`, `assigned`, ...\n\nWhat about `props`, `extra-props`, `properties`, ...? `/host/dev` is already a device but only has the standard and HVC-verifiable device properties (`\u003creg\u003e`, `\u003ciommus\u003e`) while the node this phandle points to holds all the other properties.",
