      "writtenOn": "2023-12-14T16:53:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e The node is also used for unprotected VM where pvmfw isn\u0027t involved.\n\u003e How? I thought pvIOMMUs were only supported by pKVM for pVMs? What is parsing the VM DTBO\u0027s /host, other than pvmfw?\n\nI thought that crosvm/kvm read the property for assigning device node to unprotected VM. Am I misunderstanding, and does unprotected VM access host device directly with physical address/IOMMUs?\n\n\u003e \u003e device seems better fit compared to target, virtual, overlay, assigned, ...\n\n\u003e What about props, extra-props, properties, ...? /host/dev is already a device but only has the standard and HVC-verifiable device properties (\u003creg\u003e, \u003ciommus\u003e) while the node this phandle points to holds all the other properties.\n\nI\u0027m sorry but I don\u0027t have a good idea. Honestly, I can\u0027t even tell what\u0027s better and/or worse. Would you discuss with other people in UK about the naming? Otherwise I\u0027ll just use `android,pvmfw,target` for now because nobody complaint about your initial naming `target`. We can change the naming later if it becomes problem.",
      "parentUuid": "7ec30101_8b240049",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fde5196c8f4a3fea66a3f634edcd234bd88e378e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
