      "writtenOn": "2023-12-14T17:07:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I thought that crosvm/kvm read the property for assigning device node to unprotected VM.\n\nNo, CrosVM doesn\u0027t parse `/host` and doesn\u0027t \"understand\" the content of the `__overlay__` nodes: it simply applies the DTBO, blindly.\n\n\u003e does unprotected VM access host device directly with physical address/IOMMUs?\n\nNo, in \"regular\" KVM, guests still access the device MMIO through VAs and map/unmap DMA by relying on ioctls issued by the VMM to VFIO. Those ioctls are typically issued from a back-end pvIOMMU such as `virtio-iommu` but I\u0027m not sure we have all the plumbing in place in crosvm to even support that? Anyway, the pKVM pvIOMMUs wouldn\u0027t get spawned, AFAIK.\n\n\u003e Otherwise I\u0027ll just use `android,pvmfw,target` for now because nobody complaint about your initial naming `target`.\n\nSure, I should\u0027ve thought more than a second about the name before writing that one down!\n\n\u003e We can change the naming later if it becomes problem.\n\nThe longer we wait, the harder it\u0027ll become (and will be impossible once the ABI is released).",
      "parentUuid": "a357c0f6_ab90287e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 26,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "fde5196c8f4a3fea66a3f634edcd234bd88e378e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
